          <font size="-1">
            <i>Katia writes:</i>
<br><br>
As patch day arrived, guilds from all over scrambled to their targets. Our east-coasters and habitants of the Atlantic Ocean started the day off with a King Tormax kill. Then, the Itraer Vius died shortly afterwards. The night was still young for many of us, so we moved to Ssra and tore the High Priest a new asshole. 
<br>
<br>
<center>
<img src="images/highpriest">
</center>
<br>
<br>
Whew. Three targets in one night was a lot, especially with all the competition on the server. However, that wasn't going to stop us. We moved to Kael and finally finished Velious. The Avatar of War died as a <b>GUILD FIRST</b> in a nearly perfect execution. I've never seen so much guildspam after a dead mob before...what an exhilarating fight!
<p>
<center><img src="images/rude-aow.jpg" border="0" alt=",,|,,(^_^),,|,, AoW"></center>
<br>
<br>
Four targets down -- two of them relatively new to the guild. So now, you'd think we'd be exhausted by now. WRONG! Our scouts confirmed that the Shei Vinitras was up, so we moved to Akheva and...well...I think Dendrite puts it best here:
<center>
<br>
<br>
<img src="images/densv">
<br>
<br>
<a href="images/Shei">
<img src=images/Shei width="341" height="255" border="0">
</a>
</center>
<p>
Another <b>GUILD FIRST</b> and possibly server-wide first: Shei dead AFTER AoW and High Priest :P, but yadda 
yadda...that's getting old.
<br>
<br>
The guild was rolling and just didn't want to stop! Our extreme-team west-coasters kept the ball rolling, and we managed to kill <u>Yelinak</u> and <u>Dain Frostreaver IV</u> before finally hitting the sack. In summary: 7 targets down:<br>
<ul>
<li>The Avatar of War</li>
<li>Shei Vinitras</li>
<li>High Priest of Ssraeshza</li>
<li>King Tormax</li>
<li>Yelinak</li>
<li>Dain Frostreaver IV</li>
<li>Itraer Vius</li>
</ul>
<p>
I think I can speak for all of us when I say: "WTB SLEEP!"

